From 286c5c0986a46977e5bcd0a5fb771930716f65f5 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Thu, 8 Oct 2026 16:44:14 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 06/13] fuzz_arrange: --dfirst applies every field of the
 variant

The --dfirst loop copied the variant's fc / mrv / support / min_words /
gather / cross into the options but not its pretest or fixw fields, so
the pt_* variants (and fixw, w5_fixw) ran the V_d searches with the
default pretest and per-r1 widths: the d-first fuzz never exercised the
pretest from 1-4 vectors placed, nor the single-width root, under the
top-label root. Set opts.pretest_min and opts.r1_width there as in the
plain loop.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01GSaYLGdzq6d82nBLeSZFgB
---
 src/c/fuzz_arrange.c | 3 +++
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/c/fuzz_arrange.c b/src/c/fuzz_arrange.c
index 6c24db0..21a7c88 100644
--- a/src/c/fuzz_arrange.c
+++ b/src/c/fuzz_arrange.c
@@ -1366,6 +1366,9 @@ int main(int argc, char **argv) {
       o.min_words = V->min_words;
       o.gather = V->gather;
       o.cross = V->cross;
+      o.r1_width = !V->fixw;
+      if (V->pretest)
+        o.pretest_min = V->pretest > 0 ? V->pretest : 0;
       fails += dfirst_check(seed, &l, &o, V->name, (int)(seed / NVAR % 2));
       total_sq += oracle_out.k;
       inst_with_sq += oracle_out.k > 0;
